## DEV responses to open questions

**Q1 — Model storage location (`~/.ollama`):** Was a deliberate design decision that turned out
to be wrong from a user perspective. FIXED in `9ddea46`: `_child_env()` now sets `OLLAMA_MODELS`
to `writable_root() / "models"` = `%LOCALAPPDATA%\KimCad\models`. The uninstaller's existing
`DelTree({localappdata}\KimCad)` prompt covers them. The reuse-system-Ollama path is unaffected
(that path never calls `_child_env`; system Ollama uses its own dir).

**Q2 — Down-state wording ("Make sure Ollama is running"):** FIXED in `9ddea46`:
`MODEL_UNAVAILABLE_MESSAGE` now reads "the engine isn't running — restart from Settings, then
try again." No "Ollama" anywhere the managed-AI user will see.

**Q3 — Reuse-of-system-Ollama path (not tested this run):** Confirmed by architecture: if
`find_system_ollama()` returns a path, `ensure_serving()` uses it directly without calling
`_child_env()`, so the managed-engine path (with `OLLAMA_MODELS` pinned) is never entered.
The real-tool test in `test_ollama_runtime_real.py` covers the spawn/teardown branch; the
reuse branch is covered by `test_ensure_serving_reuses_already_up_server`. Full live reuse
will be verified on a box with a system Ollama in a future run.

**Q4 — Silent install:** Acceptable per directive heads-up (GUI automation isn't drivable
unattended on the tester harness). The directive explicitly permitted it as an automation
fallback. The app under test was the real installed product; method disclosed in the report.

